Among the three candidates, 2result.sql is the only one that

• scans ALL 31 daily tables for December 2020,  
• extracts ga_session_id, source and medium from event_params (with sensible fall‑backs),  
• de‑duplicates sessions correctly (user_pseudo_id + ga_session_id), and  
• maps those sessions to the full set of default channel‑group rules (so Organic Search sessions are not mis‑labelled as “Unassigned”, unlike 0result.sql; 1result.sql puts everything into “Unassigned”).

Because of this more accurate classification, 2result.sql delivers the correct per‑channel session totals.

